{
  "summary": "Senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore of the Nick Xenophon Team (NXT) announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after confirming she holds dual British citizenship by descent through her mother, who was born in Singapore (a former British colony) and automatically acquired 'citizenship of the United Kingdom and Colonies,' later transitioning to British citizenship under the 1983 British Nationality Act. Kakoschke-Moore, born in Darwin in 1985, inherited this citizenship despite previously believing she was not eligible—based on outdated advice her father received from the British embassy in Oman when she was 12. Describing the discovery as 'extremely surprising' and expressing she was 'heartbroken,' she plans to refer the vacancy to the High Court to determine the method of replacement. While she intends to remain with the NXT and seek re-election to the Senate, the likely outcome—a recount of the 2016 Senate ballot—could see NXT candidate Tim Storrer elected. However, NXT leader Nick Xenophon noted legal uncertainty surrounding the vacancy process, citing the recent High Court ruling in the Hollie Hughes case, and stated the party has preliminary advice suggesting a recount may not apply, calling the situation 'uncharted legal territory.' Xenophon expressed the party was 'devastated' but confident Kakoschke-Moore’s political career is not over."
}
```

